Mosaico FluidBox derives its simulation, particle renderer, and firmware
integration from:
V4C38/esp32-fluidbox, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 V4C38.
Source: https://github.com/V4C38/esp32-fluidbox
Upstream commit: 21d7516d143da25bab9176257131d01a66a2573d.
The MIT license text and copyright notice are retained in LICENSE.
Local modifications include Mosaico hardware support, simulation parameters
and particle foam, additional rendering modes, and a TE-synchronized display
pipeline with PSRAM frame buffers.

The CO5300 initialization sequence in main/display.c is adapted from:
esp-mosaico/esp-mosaico-bsp, via eMUQI/QuotaFrame.
Copyright 2026 Espressif Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD.
Licensed under Apache-2.0; see licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.
Source: https://github.com/esp-mosaico/esp-mosaico-bsp
Source file: components/esp-mosaico-bsp/onboard/display.c.
The sequence has been adapted to a standalone DMA renderer without LVGL.
The modified display implementation uses TE synchronization, PSRAM frame
buffers, and band transfers scheduled after the panel scan passes each band.
QuotaFrame reference commit: 4c1aa477a340fc100003e892b2ecba292c77bb9e.
BSP original commit: 392860b1d1a123c3377947074b2af1f600e86c5d.

CABadge port source: eMUQI/esp-mosaico-fluidbox
Commit: 75d0c076b3f5b3529253f9238bc936875c47a159.
Port changes: 360x360 circular case, PSRAM BSS, native RGB565 LVGL images,
SC7A20 acceleration input without gyroscope, touch controls and task lifecycle.
Only simulation/rendering/configuration files are imported. The CO5300
initialization sequence, main/display.c, BMI270 driver and TE pipeline
described above are not included; CABadge uses its existing display adapter.
